# API Conventions

**Base URL:** `https://indusjs-fleet-docker-960880113496.asia-south2.run.app/api/v2`

## Request pattern
```kotlin
httpClient.get("$baseUrl/endpoint") {
    headers { append(HttpHeaders.Authorization, "Bearer $token") }
    url { parameters.append("start_date", startDate) }
}
```

## Response wrapper
```kotlin
@Serializable
data class ApiResponse<T>(
    @SerialName("success") val success: Boolean,
    @SerialName("data") val data: T,
    @SerialName("message") val message: String? = null
)
```

## Date formats in API
| Context | Format | Example |
|---------|--------|---------|
| Trip scheduling | ISO 8601 | `2026-03-14T15:30:00Z` |
| Cost entries | DD-MM-YYYY | `14-03-2026` |
| Documents | DD-MM-YYYY | `14-03-2026` |
| Query params (reports) | YYYY-MM-DD | `2026-03-14` |

## Auth
- Bearer token in `Authorization` header on every request
- Token stored via `UserLocalDataSource.getAuthToken()`
- 401 response → automatic logout via `AuthenticationManager`
